# Component Naming & File Organization

## Naming Convention Priority
**Prioritize component type over specificity** for better alphabetical organization:

### Good Examples:
- `card-user` instead of `user-card`
- `card-image` instead of `image-card`
- `button-primary` instead of `primary-button`
- `form-login` instead of `login-form`

### Directory Structure
When many similar components are created, consider creating a dedicated directory:
- `/components/card/` - for all card-related components
- `/components/button/` - for all button-related components
- `/components/form/` - for all form-related components

## File Organization

### Pages vs Components
- **Pages** (no selector, direct route access) go in `/pages/` directory
- **Reusable components** go in `/components/` directory
- **Pages should be "dumb"** - contain minimal logic, only display components
- **All business logic should be in components**, not pages

### Component Placement
When creating a component in `/components/`, check the directory tree structure to find the best place:
- Look for existing similar components
- Consider creating subdirectories for related components
- Follow the established pattern in the codebase

## File Naming
- Use kebab-case for file names: `card-customer-row.component.ts`
- Use PascalCase for class names: `CardCustomerRowComponent`
- Use kebab-case for selectors: `app-card-customer-row`

## Example Structure
```
/components/
  /card/
    card-user/
      card-user.component.ts
      card-user.component.html
      card-user.component.scss
    card-image/
      card-image.component.ts
      card-image.component.html
      card-image.component.scss
  /button/
    button-primary/
    button-secondary/
```
